All four cases work as expected. Here's what the program demonstrates:

**`GetTypeInfo<T>()`** — returns a strongly-typed `JsonTypeInfo<T>` directly (no cast needed). Used it to serialize a `Person`.

**`TryGetTypeInfo<T>()`** — probes for metadata without throwing:
- Against a reflection-based resolver → `true` for `Person`
- Against a source-gen context that only knows `Person` → `false` for `Widget`

The key .NET 11 APIs:

```csharp
// Typed retrieval (throws if unavailable)
JsonTypeInfo<Person> info = options.GetTypeInfo<Person>();

// Safe probe (returns bool, no exception)
if (options.TryGetTypeInfo<Widget>(out JsonTypeInfo<Widget>? info)) { ... }
```

